1. Kubernetes GitOps & CI/CD Stack
    - GitOps Tools
        GitOps means:
            Git repository = source of truth
            Kubernetes cluster state is continuously reconciled from Git
            Changes happen via pull requests instead of manual kubectl commands
        The two dominant GitOps tools are:

2. Argo CD
    Argo CD Official Site
    What it is
        A Kubernetes-native GitOps continuous delivery tool.
    Argo CD:
        Watches Git repositories
        Detects changes
        Syncs Kubernetes manifests/Helm charts/Kustomize
        Applies them to clusters automatically
    Features
        Web UI
        RBAC
        Multi-cluster support
        Helm support
        Kustomize support
        Rollbacks
        Drift detection
        Application health monitoring
    Best for
        Teams wanting a strong UI
        Enterprise Kubernetes platforms
        Easier observability and debugging
        Application-centric deployments
    Typical Workflow
        Developer pushes code
                ↓
        CI builds Docker image
                ↓
        CI updates Kubernetes manifests in Git
                ↓
        ArgoCD detects Git change
                ↓
        ArgoCD syncs cluster automatically

3. Flux CD
    Flux CD Official Site
    What it is
        A lightweight GitOps toolkit for Kubernetes.
    Flux is more:
        Modular
        Kubernetes-native
        CLI/operator driven
    Features
        Helm support
        Kustomize support
        OCI support
        Image automation
        Multi-tenancy
        Progressive delivery integrations
    Best for
        Platform engineering teams
        Kubernetes-native workflows
        Minimalist setups
        Advanced GitOps automation
    Typical Workflow
        Developer pushes code
                ↓
        CI builds/pushes image
                ↓
        Flux updates manifests automatically
                ↓
        Cluster reconciles desired state

4. Argo CD vs Flux CD
    Feature	            Argo CD	                Flux CD
    UI	                Excellent built-in UI	Minimal
    Learning curve	    Easier	                More Kubernetes-centric
    Architecture	    App-focused	            Toolkit/operator-focused
    GitOps style	    Pull-based	            Pull-based
    Helm/Kustomize	    Yes	                    Yes
    Multi-cluster	    Strong	                Strong
    Enterprise adoption	Very high	            Very high
    CNCF	            Graduated	            Graduated

5. Quick Recommendation
    - Choose Argo CD if:
        You want visualization/UI
        Easier onboarding
        Simpler operations
    - Choose Flux if:
        You prefer pure Kubernetes-native tooling
        Want modular automation
        Have strong platform engineering maturity

7. CI/CD Tools
    - GitOps tools are usually paired with CI systems.
    - The CI system:
        Tests code
        Builds Docker images
        Pushes images
        Updates GitOps manifests
    - Then GitOps deploys.

8. GitHub Actions
    GitHub Actions Docs
    What it is
        CI/CD integrated into GitHub.
    Common Kubernetes Workflow
        - Run tests
        - Build Docker image
        - Push to Docker Hub/ECR/GCR
        - Update Helm values.yaml
        - Commit changes to GitOps repo
    Strengths
        Excellent GitHub integration
        Easy setup
        Great for open-source
        Marketplace actions
        Good Docker/K8s ecosystem
    Best for
        GitHub-hosted repositories
        Small → enterprise teams
        Simpler DevOps workflows

9. GitLab CI/CD
    GitLab CI/CD Docs
    What it is
    Built-in CI/CD inside GitLab.
    Strengths
        Complete DevSecOps platform
        Integrated container registry
        Security scanning
        Kubernetes integrations
        Strong self-hosting support
    Best for
        Enterprises
        Self-hosted infrastructure
        All-in-one DevOps platform
    End-to-End GitOps Architecture
        Typical Production Setup
        Developer
        ↓
        Git Push
        ↓
        CI Pipeline (GitHub Actions / GitLab CI)
        ↓
        Run Tests
        ↓
        Build Docker Image
        ↓
        Push Image Registry
        ↓
        Update Helm/Kustomize Git Repo
        ↓
        ArgoCD / Flux detects changes
        ↓
        Kubernetes cluster syncs automatically
    
10. Recommended Stack Patterns
    - Startup / Small Team
        GitHub Actions
        Argo CD
        Helm
        Docker Hub
    Simple and productive.
    - Enterprise Platform
        GitLab CI
        Flux CD
        Helm + Kustomize
        EKS/GKE/AKS
        Vault + External Secrets
    More scalable and policy-driven.

